---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
import { u } from '../lib/url';
---
<Base title={`Privacy: How ${SITE.name} Keeps Your Photos on Your Device`} description={`${SITE.name} processes photos entirely in your browser. No uploads, no accounts. Here's exactly what happens to your files and what network requests the site makes.`}>
  <div class="container" style="padding-top:32px">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href={u('/')}>Home</a> / <span aria-current="page">Privacy</span></nav>
    <article class="prose">
      <h1>Your photos never leave your device</h1>
      <p class="muted small">Last updated 31 October 2026</p>
      <p>{SITE.name} is built so that we <strong>can’t</strong> see your photos, not just so that we promise not to. All tools run as JavaScript in your browser. There is no server that receives files.</p>

      <h2>What happens when you add a photo</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Your browser reads the file from your device into memory.</li>
        <li>JavaScript on this page parses the metadata (EXIF, IPTC, XMP, ICC) and shows it to you.</li>
        <li>When you clean a photo, a new file is built in memory and saved through your browser’s normal download.</li>
        <li>When you close or reload the page, everything is gone. Nothing is stored.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Network requests this site makes</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Request</th><th>When</th><th>Contains your photo or its data?</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Page, scripts and styles from {SITE.url.replace('https://', '')}</td><td>When you open a page</td><td>No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Visit statistics (Cloudflare Web Analytics)</td><td>When you open a page</td><td>No personal data or photos: page address, referring site, browser and country</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sample photos</td><td>Only if you click “Try a sample”</td><td>No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>OpenStreetMap map tiles</td><td>Only if you click “Show map”</td><td>No photo is sent. The tile requests reveal roughly which area is being viewed.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>There are no ads or cross-site trackers on the tool pages. The only outside script is the cookie-free visit counter described below, which never sees your photos. The site sends a strict <code>Content-Security-Policy</code> header that stops scripts from sending data anywhere else.</p>

      <h2>Verify it yourself</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Go offline</strong>: load a tool page, turn on airplane mode, then add a photo. It still works.</li>
        <li><strong>Watch the network</strong>: open your browser’s developer tools → Network tab, then add a photo. No upload request appears.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Affiliate links and app links</h2>
      <p>Some pages recommend products through plain affiliate links, and link to our own iPhone apps. Clicking one takes you to the partner’s website, which then applies its own privacy policy. These links carry no information about your photos. A short tag only tells the partner which page of ours you came from. See our <a href={u('/disclosure/')}>affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
      <p>On iPhone and iPad, Safari may show a small banner for our app at the top of the page. It is generated by Safari from a single tag on the page and loads nothing from third parties.</p>

      <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>The site sets no cookies. We count visits with <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>, which does not use cookies or local storage and does not follow you across websites. It records the page address you opened, the site you came from, your browser type and country, so we can see which tools are useful. It never receives your photos or file data.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions or a security concern? Contact {SITE.author} via the <a href={u('/about/')}>About page</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
